==Calculations==
===Armor Values===
Steel Fiber gives additional Armor based on the frame's Base Armor.

The Total Armor can be calculated by the following formula:<br />
{{MathText|Total Armor {{eql}} BaseArmor {{mul}} (1 + SteelFiberPercent)}}

Example - 190 Base Armor with 100% Steel Fiber would be calculated as follows:<br />
{{MathText|Total Armor {{eql}} 190 {{mul}} (1 + 1) {{eql}} 399 Total Armor}}

===Damage Mitigation===
Damage Mitigation is the amount off the total damage that armor reduces, and is calculated as:<br />
{{MathText|Damage Mitigation {{eql}} Total Armor {{div}} (Total Armor + 300)}}<br />
The following table shows the net Damage Mitigation percentage values provided by armor for different key base armors that various frames have. 

